Understanding feedback
Why analyze review text beyond star averages?
Short answer: The text reveals why ratings happen—what delights, what drags, and how you compare.

Long answer: A 4.5 average tells you things are going well, but not which experiences create that result. Reading the language at scale exposes patterns—recurring praise for a product, consistent friction at check‑in, or differences between locations. Those insights guide operations (fix bottlenecks), training (replicate what’s praised), and marketing (highlight strengths customers actually mention).

Why it matters
It turns unstructured text into operational priorities and marketing themes.
What to do
Read patterns at scale instead of relying on anecdotes.
